{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01PuCHpbpApca2vVY64MM1ci","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test is failing because the replacement effect doesn't properly exile the spell after it resolves. Let me debug this.\n\nThe issue is: when the trigger resolves, it calls `cast_spell_free` from the graveyard. The spell goes to the stack. Then `_resolve_top_of_stack` resolves the spell. After resolving, `_resolve_spell` in casting.py moves the spell to the graveyard. The replacement effect should intercept this.\n\nBut the replacement effect is registered with `source=archaic` (the Dawning Archaic). When the replacement effect fires, it should redirect the destination.\nLooking at the casting code, when a spell resolves, it checks if it's a permanent type and moves it to the battlefield, otherwise it moves from the stack to the graveyard via `move_to_zone`. The problem is that replacement effects might not be getting consulted properly during this zone transition.\n\nI'm realizing the replacement effect check in `move_to_zone` only applies when leaving the battlefield, but `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` should trigger when moving to the graveyard from anywhere. Let me trace through the logic more carefully to see where the replacement check actually happens. The issue is that instant and sorcery spells moving from the stack to the graveyard don't trigger a replacement event the way creatures do, so the replacement effect won't fire. I need to intercept the spell resolution instead—the cleanest approach is to modify the spell's resolve callback to check for the exile flag after it resolves and handle the graveyard movement accordingly. Looking at how replacement effects work in zones.py, I see they're only applied when leaving the battlefield with a replacement event, but moving a spell from the stack to the graveyard doesn't trigger this. The proper solution is to pass a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` from `_resolve_spell` so replacement effects can intercept non-permanent spells going to the graveyard.\n\nWriting the replacement event handler... applying replacement effects before moving the card. The replacement event needs to reference the specific card being moved, but the base event class doesn't have a `card` attribute that works properly — I'd need to either use a subclass or set the field directly on the event instance.\n\nI'm considering a simpler approach instead: mark the spell with a flag before casting it, then check for that flag in a trigger that fires when the spell is cast, and use that to handle the card draw effect without relying on the replacement event system.\n\nActually, the cleanest solution is to create a specialized event subclass that properly handles the card reference, so the replacement condition can check if the card being moved to the graveyard is the spell itself. Completing the zone movement logic and updating the replacement condition for the spell event. I'm realizing the current `_resolve_spell` doesn't actually apply replacement effects when moving spells to the graveyard, which is why the exile-instead effect won't work—I need to wire up the event application there first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":809,"cache_read_input_tokens":132028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":809},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"02b16798-ad58-4640-86bc-9064b595557c","request_id":"req_011CbwDBPSEziFrPdSho7zsm"}
