{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_019HYvcqCP1RNhZDuy2UFwpV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see a potential issue: `apply_all` resets objects using `_reset_characteristics()`. For the land (which is a CardImpl subclass but not a Creature), `_reset_characteristics` would reset `card_types` back to just `{CardType.LAND}`. This would undo the animation!\n\nLet me check `CardImpl._reset_characteristics`:\n```python\ndef _reset_characteristics(self) -> None:\n    self.card_types = set(self._original_card_types)\n    self.keywords = self._original_keywords\n```\n\nThe `_original_card_types` is set during `__init__` as a frozen copy of the initial card types. Since we set `card_types` to `{CardType.LAND}` in the Land subclass, `_original_card_types` captures just that. When `_reset_characteristics` is called, it reverts `card_types` back to `{CardType.LAND}`, losing the CREATURE type we added. The same problem happens with `modified_power` getting reset to `base_power`.\n\nThe real issue is that each time `apply_all` is called, the animation gets undone. The pump trigger's ContinuousEffect runs its `apply` function after the reset, so `modified_power` gets incremented again, but `card_types` stays stuck at just `{LAND}` — the CREATURE type never comes back.\n\nThe fix is to make the animation itself a permanent continuous effect. That way when `apply_all` resets everything, it'll re-apply the animation effect (which adds CREATURE and sets P/T to 2/4), and then the pump effect can layer its +1/+0 on top correctly. adds CREATURE type through a permanent continuous effect, which is the proper MTG model for animation. The pump effect then applies a separate end-of-turn continuous effect for the P/T boost. But since `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex` extends `Land` rather than `Creature`, I need to ensure the power and toughness attributes are properly initialized when animating. I see the issue now — the pump effect's `+= 1` would keep accumulating across multiple `apply_all` calls because `modified_power` never gets reset for Land cards. I need to override `_reset_characteristics` in the Great Hall implementation to reset the power and toughness back to their base values, then layer the continuous effects properly: one at TYPE to re-add CREATURE after the reset, and another at POWER_TOUGHNESS to apply the pump.\n\nRestructuring the implementation...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":150885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"534ed0db-cd72-418a-8bdb-4707bdafc1e3","request_id":"req_011CbwDWTWbGnmtk4V2qjy9H"}
