{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JiQPTrepXGKrzMgbvBJMwk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very clear model to follow from Etali, Primal Storm.\n\nKey differences for Improvisation Capstone:\n1. Exile from library until MV >= 4 (not just top card)\n2. The effect is in `on_resolve` (Sorcery), not a trigger\n3. Paradigm: after resolution, exile self and cast copy at beginning of each main phase\n\nFor the MV calculation:\n```python\nmana_cost = getattr(card, 'mana_cost', None)\nmv = mana_cost.cmc if mana_cost else 0\n```\n\nNow I'm setting up the class structure with the mana cost of 5R2, using a shared mutable list to track paradigm registration across shallow copies.\n\n```\n\nImplementing the resolution logic: I'm getting the controller's library and exile zone, then exiling cards from the top of the library until their combined mana values reach at least 4, tracking each card as it's moved. After that, the player gets to cast any of those exiled cards.\n\n```\nI'm setting up a replacement effect to redirect spells that would go to the graveyard into exile instead, using a condition function to check if the spell is the card in question and a replacement function that changes the destination zone.\n```\n    ))\n    \n    # Register recurring trigger for each precombat main\n    _register_paradigm_trigger(game, card, controller)\n\n\ndef _register_paradigm_trigger(game, exiled_card, controller):\n    \"\"\"Register recurring trigger: at beginning of each of controller's main phases, \n    may cast a copy of exiled_card for free.\"\"\"\n    from engine.events import BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\n    from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n    import copy as _copy\n    from engine.stack import StackObject\n    \n    source = object()  # sentinel for unregistration if needed\n    \n    def _condition(g, event):\n        return g.active_player is controller\n    \n    def _effect(g):\n        try:\n            if not controller.choose_yes_no(f\"Cast a copy of {exiled_card.name} for free?\"):\n```\n\nDefining the trigger effect...\n\nWhen the copy resolves, it goes through the full card resolution including the exile effect, but the shared `_paradigm_registered` flag prevents it from re-registering the trigger. The copy doesn't move zones like the original does, it just executes the resolve logic directly. I should check if there are any edge cases with the exiled card being captured in the closure. about the zone movement functions — `move_zone` is the low-level operation that checks if the object exists in the source zone, while `move_to_zone` is the higher-level wrapper that handles replacement effects. For exiling library cards, I should probably use `move_to_zone` like Etali does, passing the library and exile zones as arguments.\n\nWriting the implementation...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":52104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1064},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"205599bd-9790-4bbb-9e2a-a3721f0a0471","request_id":"req_011CbwE9hPJmRm9dn1nLQMRR"}
