{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01G5xyyBp4hWQXxy38v89u1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, now I have the pattern for ETB triggers. Let me think about sos_13 carefully:\n\n1. **EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares** — Creature {1}{W}{W}, 3/3, Cat Cleric, Legendary\n   - Name: \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\"\n   - ETB: target player creates a 1/1 white-black Inkling token with flying\n   - Then if opponent controls more creatures → becomes prepared\n   - While prepared: may cast copy of Swords to Plowshares (exile target creature; controller gains life = its power)\n   - Casting that copy unprepares the creature\n\n2. **SwordsToPlowshares** — Instant {W}\n   - Exile target creature; its controller gains life equal to its power\n\nThe \"prepared\" mechanic is a state flag on the creature that lets the player cast a copy of the Swords instant from exile using the free casting mechanism, and casting it removes the prepared state.\n\nThe implementation flow creates a new Swords instance, sets up ownership, adds it to exile, casts it for free, then unprepares the creature. But the tricky part is that this isn't just a one-time effect at entry — it's an ongoing ability that the player can activate whenever the creature is prepared and they have priority, similar to an activated ability. The oracle text suggests it works at sorcery speed since it's copying a sorcery, though I need to verify whether Swords to Plowshares is actually an instant or sorcery. I'll expose this through `get_activated_abilities()` where the cost function checks if the creature is prepared, and the effect creates a free copy of Swords to Plowshares in exile and casts it. Writing the ability implementation... I need to handle the case where `cast_spell_free` fails — if there's no valid target for Swords to Plowshares, the cast will throw an exception and I shouldn't unprepare the source. Let me move the unprepare logic to happen only after a successful cast. I'm also checking how `cast_spell_free` handles targeting to make sure the spell can properly select its targets. Reviewing the full function...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1862,"cache_read_input_tokens":78786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1862},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"041e5836-8e7f-4fed-a7e1-b0b175b34a4f","request_id":"req_011CbwETA2f1sbRZZMQxo9SV"}
