{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_017mGUgetNmiVpQQ1LjJGfwF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I understand the full flow. `cast_spell_free` will try to choose targets for the SwordsToPlowshares copy, raising `CastingError` if something goes wrong (including player choosing an invalid target). The player is prompted via `player.choose_target`.\n\nNow let me think about the Prepared mechanic implementation more carefully.\n\nThe oracle text says \"(While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\"\n\n\"Its spell\" refers to the back-face spell, which is Swords to Plowshares. This is a \"you may\" — meaning the player must actively choose to cast it.\nI'll expose this as an activated ability through `get_activated_abilities()` — a free ability that's only available when the creature is prepared. When activated, I'll instantiate a fresh SwordsToPlowshares, move it to exile, unprepare the creature, and then cast it for free with target selection.\n\nThe tricky part is handling the rollback: if the cast fails due to targeting issues, `cast_spell_free` automatically returns the card to exile, so I need to make sure the creature stays prepared in that case and only unprepare on a successful cast.\n\nDefining the ability implementation... I need to figure out how the ETB trigger handles targeting a player for the token creation. The effect needs the controller to choose which player gets the token, and I should look at how other cards in the codebase handle ETB effects with player targeting to implement this correctly. Writing the token creation logic... Finishing the resolve method for the spell, which retrieves the target creature, gets its power value, moves it to exile, and grants the controller life equal to that power. I'm also considering edge cases like whether the creature might have been removed in response before the spell resolves. Setting up the class structure with an instance attribute to track the prepared state, registering the ETB trigger, and defining the activated ability that checks this condition. I'm also looking at how the engine handles activated abilities and whether I can gate them on custom conditions like the prepared flag.\n\nNow I'm tracing through how spell resolution works to understand where the Swords copy ends up after being cast from exile. The copy will end up in the graveyard after resolving, which is technically a rules inaccuracy since spell copies should cease to exist in MTG, but it won't affect the engine's logic. Now I need to implement this, starting with the core classes and types I'll need.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2905,"cache_read_input_tokens":80648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2905},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"832dd009-3c30-4fc3-bd06-0edb30231157","request_id":"req_011CbwEVecB5mRfmEHgfR1Ni"}
