{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01QHCfjV1KpwMGujrFeh69YT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test for `test_becomes_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` fails. Let me debug this.\n\nThe issue: when ETB fires, it creates an Inkling token for the target player. After creating the Inkling, the creature count is updated. So after the Inkling is created for p0:\n- p0: emeritus (1) + inkling (1) = 2 creatures\n- p1: opp_creature1 (1) + opp_creature2 (1) = 2 creatures\n\nSo after creating the token, p0 and p1 both have 2 creatures, and p1 is NOT strictly more. \n\nThe prepared condition is evaluated after the token gets created, so by that point p0 has 2 creatures and p1 has 2 creatures—they're equal, not in the opponent's favor, which is why the test fails.\n\nI need to adjust the test so the Inkling goes to p1 instead of p0. That way p0 stays at 1 creature while p1 reaches 3, satisfying the prepared condition. I'm modifying the script to target p1 as the player receiving the token.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":92303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1046},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"9edd7a52-098f-41b1-85ef-9ae106f1ddab","request_id":"req_011CbwEejh24QeoELKoGbC7W"}
