{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_016CecSgxStPR2UH9AA2SjRN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so when a loyalty ability is activated:\n1. The `StackObject` is pushed with `on_resolve=ability.effect`\n2. `ability.effect` receives `game` when called\n\nSo the effect function gets `game` as its only argument. There's no `targets` parameter. The effect has to get targets from the planeswalker itself (e.g., `pw._resolve_target` or `pw.chosen_targets`).\n\nBut the TODO says to use `self.chosen_targets`. Let me check how `chosen_targets` is set...\nI'm realizing the activation flow doesn't actually have a targeting step, so `chosen_targets` might be empty when the effect runs. I need to trace through how targets are actually being resolved — maybe `_resolve_target` is set elsewhere in the flow, or I'm missing where the targeting happens for loyalty abilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":124765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":598},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"8a7814f5-6641-4066-8bc6-584bcb6445c4","request_id":"req_011CbwF7HKWw8v3xyxdBApLF"}
