{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_013qkQmsbeWb2CTBqK8FSuVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `LoyaltyAbilityInstance.effect` is just `(game) -> None`. There's no targeting built into the loyalty ability activation. So for abilities that need targets, the effect function itself should query for targets from `pw.chosen_targets` (if that's set by the casting pipeline) or prompt the player.\n\nLooking at the TODO: \"do not use `_resolve_target` / `_resolve_targets`\" and \"read this card's targets from `self.chosen_targets`, which the engine sets from the activation's targets\".\n\nBut the activation doesn't set `chosen_targets`... \n\nI'm wondering if `chosen_targets` gets populated when the planeswalker is cast, though that doesn't make sense since planeswalkers themselves aren't targeted. Let me trace through the Chandra implementation to see where `_resolve_target` is actually being set, and check what happens in the priority loop when a loyalty ability activates.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1492,"cache_read_input_tokens":125363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1492},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d92b6c43-7322-4b8d-bfe2-1d1f7f4c24eb","uuid":"c6de889a-16b6-40f3-bcbd-3b251ab50ebc","request_id":"req_011CbwF7zs68feS5wUig8yrH"}
